This workspace is the model harness. Cline must use the harness gateway, not raw Spark or M5 ports.

Gateway: http://127.0.0.1:8787/v1
API key: sk-harness-local  (or harness-local)
Default model: harness-local

Roles:
- harness-local  Spark e10b Qwen3-Coder-Next (worker — default)
- harness-dgx2   Spark 49af Qwen3-Coder-Next (new DGX, :8900 on .45)
- harness-asus   ASUS gx10-fc2e Qwen3-Coder-Next (:8900 on .46)
- harness-dgx3   Spark 69c8 Qwen3-Coder-Next (new DGX, :8900 on .49)
- harness-m5     M5 Qwen3.8-27B (orchestrator / screenshots, short packets only)
- harness-frontier  Claude (senior). Do not paste the Cline thread. Use `harness rescue PACKET.md`.
- harness-orch   Cline types here; gateway runs dispatch (M5 slice + coder pool + tester stitch). One reply. Not a Cline fan-out.
- harness-auto   dead-box failover only (connect/5xx/empty). Not a quality ladder.

Work happens via Cline Model ID `harness-orch` (gateway runs dispatch) or `harness dispatch "intent"`. `harness optimize` A/Bs the same packet on every box. Do not pick four Cline Model IDs and hope.

Do not call :8800–:8803 (embeddings) or :8902 (OCR).
Do not restart, kill, or reconfigure inference services.
Keep Cline tasks short. Do not feed 80k-token threads into a local model.
Log is automatic — every turn is written to results/harness.db table cline_turns.
